INT. VINEYARD CELLAR - BARREL ROOM - DUSK

Oak barrels in rows. Candlelight. A tasting table with four glasses.

IZABELLA ROMANO-OKAFOR, 30s, in a linen apron, pours. Across from her, THEODORE "TEDDY" GALLOWAY, 30s, her ex, swirls and sniffs. At the end of the table, her sister CAMILA ROMANO, 30s, in a sundress, studies him. And beside Camila, a quiet man, HENRIK ABASI-LUND, 40s, who has said nothing all evening.

Teddy sips. Izabella watches. Camila watches Izabella. Henrik watches the wine.

TEDDY
It's good.

IZABELLA
It's better than good.

TEDDY
It's... complex.

CAMILA
He means it's sour.

TEDDY
I do not.

CAMILA
You do. Your nose wrinkles.

Teddy touches his nose. Izabella suppresses a smile. Henrik takes a slow sip and sets down his glass.

HENRIK
It's perfect.

All three turn. He shrugs, unbothered.

HENRIK (CONT'D)
I'm the one who sold her the grapes.

IZABELLA
(to Teddy)
That's Henrik.

TEDDY
I gathered.

IZABELLA
And that's my fiance.

Teddy's glass stops halfway to his mouth. Camila lowers her eyes. Henrik, calmly, takes Izabella's hand.

TEDDY
...Congratulations.

IZABELLA
Thank you, Teddy.

He drains the glass. Sets it down. Smooths his jacket. Camila slides the bottle toward him, tender.

CAMILA
Another?

TEDDY
(a breath)
Please.
